    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Jackson Merrill** headlining the offensive unit. Boasting a 74.43 rating, he is our strongest play against Holmes, G, as the combination of a favorable SP_xERA (4.47) and a 13% dynamic platoon advantage creates an ideal ceiling for run production. **Cole Carrigg** also presents massive value at 69.15; he benefits significantly from a 14% park factor boost and a favorable matchup against the southpaw Bennett, making him a high-floor selection for our outfield. Meanwhile, **Gunnar Henderson** (68.65) and **Coby Mayo** (66.72) provide stability against Aldegheri, whose 5.75 xERA suggests he will be unable to suppress our power hitters, despite the tactical decision to neutralize **Gunnar Henderson**\u2019s projected efficiency due to the platoon disadvantage.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench today was between **Nolan Schanuel** (51.38) and **Dominic Smith** (50.08). While **Nolan Schanuel** held a slight edge in raw projection, the optimizer preferred **Dominic Smith** due to the specific platoon dynamics at play and the need to preserve our bench flexibility. **Nasim Nunez** was strongly considered for his potential stolen base impact, but his projection plummeted to 40.57 due to a unfavorable 9th-order spot and a matchup against a tough southpaw in Mayza, keeping him glued to the pine. We are closely monitoring the weather, as the heavy reliance on **Andy Pages**\u2014who carries a 63.82 rating\u2014hinges on the expectation that his elite sprint speed can exploit the slow delivery of Matthews, potentially adding to our stolen base tally. With **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (52.68) facing a tough test against Brown, H, we are counting on our middle-order depth to carry the day in the Roto standings.",
